virglrenderer 1.3.0: give the cursor's rows top first unless its resource is
y_0_top.

vrend_renderer_get_cursor_contents turns every cursor image over. A cursor the
kernel uploads from a dumb buffer is stored top row first (its transfer isn't
inverted, since it isn't y_0_top), so turning it over shows it upside down.
Turn it over only when the resource is y_0_top, the rule transfers back to the
guest follow. Scripts/build-virgl.sh applies it.

diff -ruN a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c c/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -12966,8 +12966,11 @@
       glGetTexImage(res->target, 0, format, type, data);
    }
 
+   /* crate: rows top first, as a transfer back to the guest gives them, which
+    * turns them over only for a y_0_top resource. Turning every cursor over
+    * puts a cursor uploaded from a dumb buffer upside down. */
    for (h = 0; h < res->base.height0; h++) {
-      uint32_t doff = (res->base.height0 - h - 1) * res->base.width0 * blsize;
+      uint32_t doff = (res->y_0_top ? res->base.height0 - h - 1 : h) * res->base.width0 * blsize;
       uint32_t soff = h * res->base.width0 * blsize;
 
       memcpy(data2 + doff, data + soff, res->base.width0 * blsize);
